    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3681fb17_8d382509",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_ftdi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-10T18:41:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced that using the timer interrupt is the right technical choice for the bitbanging.\nit has a high overhead.\nWhy not simply looping in the task ?",
      "revId": "e1b54fee54e71d7be73a8a5932451105d38f6403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7687f329_ef04357e",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_ftdi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112304
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-10T19:02:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I talked to Alec about looping in the task, and he was concerned that it would be pulling too much CPU from the PD.\n\nAlso, without the timer interrupt, there\u0027s no easy way to toggle the clock at a constant frequency.",
      "parentUuid": "3681fb17_8d382509",
      "revId": "e1b54fee54e71d7be73a8a5932451105d38f6403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7687f329_2f61ed15",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_ftdi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-10T21:15:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, I\u0027m more concerned this interrupt would interfere with PD communication from firing too often, that\u0027s why I was concerned about running the JTAG clock at a high frequency.\n\nThe tradeoff is with an interrupt you will get a consistent clock frequency at the expense of causing problems on PD. With a task, as long as PD priority is higher, you will have working PD, but your JTAG clock frequency will be inconsistent.\n\nI\u0027m not sure how important it is for JTAG to have a consistent clock.",
      "parentUuid": "7687f329_ef04357e",
      "revId": "e1b54fee54e71d7be73a8a5932451105d38f6403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7687f329_32d79662",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_ftdi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112304
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-10T22:20:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My bad, I must have gotten mixed up, sorry.\n\nIt sounds like I should just loop in the task then, in which case I\u0027ll just ignore the frequency sent by OpenOCD?",
      "parentUuid": "7687f329_2f61ed15",
      "revId": "e1b54fee54e71d7be73a8a5932451105d38f6403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
